---
import PhaseLayout from '../../layouts/PhaseLayout.astro';
---

<PhaseLayout title="Competitive Programming Phase 1 — Polymath.Sys" activeNav="courses">

<style>
  .cpn { display:flex; gap:0; margin-bottom:2.5rem; border:1px solid #222; width:fit-content; }
  .cpn-link { font-family:monospace; font-size:11px; letter-spacing:0.08em; text-transform:uppercase; padding:0.45rem 1.1rem; color:#555; text-decoration:none; border-right:1px solid #222; }
  .cpn-link:last-child { border-right:none; }
  .cpn-link.active { background:#111; color:#fff; }
  .cpn-link:hover:not(.active) { background:#f3f3f3; color:#111; }
  .cpn-back { display:inline-block; font-family:monospace; font-size:11px; color:#888; text-decoration:none; margin-bottom:1.2rem; letter-spacing:0.05em; }
  .cpn-back:hover { color:#111; }
</style>

  <a href="/courses/competitive-programming" class="cpn-back">&larr; Competitive Programming Overview</a>
  <div class="cpn">
    <a href="/courses/cp-phase-1" class="cpn-link active">Phase 1</a>
    <a href="/courses/cp-phase-2" class="cpn-link">Phase 2</a>
    <a href="/courses/cp-phase-3" class="cpn-link">Phase 3</a>
  </div>

  <div class="track-header">
    <div class="track-badge badge-dsa">Phase 1 &middot; Months 1-3 &middot; CF Target: 1200</div>
    <div class="track-title">Phase 1 &mdash; Building the Problem-Solving Base</div>
    <div class="track-sub">Before speed, you need correctness. Before patterns, you need fundamentals. This phase builds the algorithmic vocabulary, contest habits, and problem-solving instincts that everything else rests on. Read the handbook, grind CSES, compete weekly.</div>
  </div>

    <!-- CP Step 1: Foundations -->
    <div class="step" id="cp0">
      <div class="step-head" onclick="tog('cp0')">
        <div class="step-num num-dsa">1</div>
        <div class="step-info"><div class="step-title">CP Foundations &mdash; building the problem-solving base</div><div class="step-meta">Months 1-3 &middot; Rating target: 1200 (Codeforces)</div></div>
        <div class="step-arrow" id="a-cp0">&#9660;</div>
      </div>
      <div class="step-body" id="b-cp0">
        <div class="res-list">
          <div class="res-item">
            <div class="res-icon"><svg class="res-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 19.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 17H20"></path><path d="M6.5 2H20v20H6.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 4 19.5v-15A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 2z"></path></svg></div>
            <div class="res-content">
              <div class="res-name"><a href="https://cses.fi/book/book.pdf" target="_blank" class="res-link">Competitive Programmer's Handbook &mdash; Antti Laaksonen (free PDF) <span class="res-link-arrow">&nearr;</span></a></div>
              <div class="res-desc">The best free competitive programming textbook. 300 pages covering all essential topics: sorting, searching, dynamic programming, graph algorithms, trees, number theory, combinatorics, geometry, string algorithms, and advanced techniques. Concise, well-organized, with C++ examples. Read one chapter, solve 10 problems on that topic.</div>
              <div class="res-tags"><span class="rtag free">Free PDF</span><span class="rtag must">Essential</span><span class="rtag book">Book</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="res-item">
            <div class="res-icon"><svg class="res-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14.7 6.3a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.4l1.6 1.6a1 1 0 0 0 1.4 0l3.77-3.77a6 6 0 0 1-7.94 7.94l-6.91 6.91a2.12 2.12 0 0 1-3-3l6.91-6.91a6 6 0 0 1 7.94-7.94l-3.76 3.76z"></path></svg></div>
            <div class="res-content">
              <div class="res-name"><a href="https://cses.fi/problemset/" target="_blank" class="res-link">CSES Problem Set (free) <span class="res-link-arrow">&nearr;</span></a></div>
              <div class="res-desc">300 curated problems organized by topic, perfectly sequenced for learning. Introductory problems, sorting, searching, DP, graph, tree, math, string, geometry, and advanced. Solve all 300 and you will have covered every major CP topic. This is the best single problem set for structured CP practice.</div>
              <div class="res-tags"><span class="rtag free">Free</span><span class="rtag must">Best problem set</span><span class="rtag tool">Practice</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="res-item">
            <div class="res-icon"><svg class="res-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><polygon points="10 8 16 12 10 16 10 8"></polygon></svg></div>
            <div class="res-content">
              <div class="res-name"><a href="https://www.youtube.com/@Errichto" target="_blank" class="res-link">Errichto &mdash; Competitive Programming (YouTube) <span class="res-link-arrow">&nearr;</span></a></div>
              <div class="res-desc">One of the top competitive programmers in the world explaining problem-solving live. Contest walkthroughs, topic deep dives (DP, graphs, math), and live problem-solving sessions. His binary search and DP videos are particularly exceptional. Watch after attempting problems yourself.</div>
              <div class="res-tags"><span class="rtag free">Free</span><span class="rtag vid">YouTube</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="res-item">
            <div class="res-icon"><svg class="res-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14.7 6.3a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.4l1.6 1.6a1 1 0 0 0 1.4 0l3.77-3.77a6 6 0 0 1-7.94 7.94l-6.91 6.91a2.12 2.12 0 0 1-3-3l6.91-6.91a6 6 0 0 1 7.94-7.94l-3.76 3.76z"></path></svg></div>
            <div class="res-content">
              <div class="res-name"><a href="https://atcoder.jp/contests/abc" target="_blank" class="res-link">AtCoder Beginner Contests (ABC) <span class="res-link-arrow">&nearr;</span></a></div>
              <div class="res-desc">Weekly contests with problems A-F ranging from trivial to hard. Problems A-D are perfect for beginners. AtCoder problems are cleaner and better written than Codeforces at the easy level. Do every ABC contest for 3 months to build contest stamina and speed.</div>
              <div class="res-tags"><span class="rtag free">Free</span><span class="rtag tool">Contests</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="do-box"><b>The daily practice rule:</b> Solve 2-3 problems per day, 7 days a week. Participate in every Codeforces and AtCoder contest. After each contest, upsolve every problem you could not solve during the contest. The gap between contest performance and upsolve performance IS your growth edge.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

</PhaseLayout>
